      "The the placement lead owns the decision in no-show coverage gap; the preparer may compare, label, and route but may not approve the outcome. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. A role change should trigger a review of queue access. Preparation, comparison, and follow-up may sit with the assistant. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The no-show coverage gap close note cites the placement record, the approver, and the time of the final check. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. If two roles share a queue, mark which one decides each item. Write the authority limit into the case template. The no-show coverage gap reviewer records coverage note, the owner, and the next action in one place.",
      "## Evidence dictionary",
      "Each morning the team reviews no-show coverage gap arrivals, items waiting on the the placement lead, and items ready for a verified close. Record one next action and one due time per open item. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Escalate an item that has waited past the written threshold. A sample no-show coverage gap review checks schedule, backup roster, and the surviving value in the placement record. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Record one next action and one due time per open item. Every no-show coverage gap handoff names the placement lead and the field in the placement record that will confirm the change.",
      "## Sampling and collection",
      "If the record does not match the surviving value, stop the dependent action and log the conflict in the placement record rather than choosing the more convenient value. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. In this no-show coverage gap case, the record points to the placement record and names the placement lead as the decision owner. An escalation that ends in silence remains open. Check whether the exception came from a form, a rule, or a permission. Record who released the dependent action and when. For no-show coverage gap, compare schedule with the destination value rather than relying on a status label.",
      "## Analysis and reporting",
      "Record the no-show coverage gap close reason, the approver, and the surviving evidence reference in the same case note. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Keep the prior value so the change can be explained. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Record the close reason with the same codes used in the exception queue. For no-show coverage gap, the working file keeps schedule and backup roster beside the decision note. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Tie the close note to the original request and the final evidence. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The no-show coverage gap record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from backup roster and client notice.",
