      "Review no-show coverage gap with a sample drawn from the queue export before the meeting, so the discussion cannot drift to memorable cases. End the review with one change and one measure. Report age and dependency, not only the total count. Report a null result as clearly as a positive one. Record the sample frame, the reviewer, and the criteria. The no-show coverage gap case note should show what the placement record held at the time and who reviewed it. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Separate what was observed from what the team believes caused it. A no-show coverage gap exception keeps coverage note attached and routes the question to the placement lead.",
